    &lt;span style=&#34;color: #d1d5db;&#34;&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;time style=&#34;font-style: italic;&#34;&gt;June 30, 2026&lt;/time&gt;
  
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;📘 Topic: Access Control Models&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain:&lt;/strong&gt; D5 – Identity and Access Management&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tags:&lt;/strong&gt; #cissp&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🧾 Definition&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-definition&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-definition&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Access control models define how subjects are allowed to interact with objects based on rules, labels, roles, or attributes. They are the foundation of least-privilege and authorization design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🔑 Key Points&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-key-points&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-key-points&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DAC&lt;/strong&gt;: Owners control access; flexible but weaker and harder to enforce consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MAC&lt;/strong&gt;: The system enforces labels and rules; strong and often used in high-security environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RBAC&lt;/strong&gt;: Access is granted based on roles; common in enterprise systems and easier to manage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABAC&lt;/strong&gt;: Access is granted based on attributes such as role, location, time, device, or data classification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISSP emphasis: choose the model that fits sensitivity, scalability, and operational needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;⚠️ CISSP Insight&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-cissp-insight&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-cissp-insight&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The strongest model is not always the best fit; the right model balances security, usability, and governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Least privilege should be enforced regardless of the model selected.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;⚔️ Key Difference / Trap&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-key-difference--trap&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-key-difference--trap&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DAC vs MAC&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DAC = owner-driven access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MAC = system-enforced labels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RBAC vs ABAC&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RBAC = role-based&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ABAC = role + context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 Keywords:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Role → RBAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time / Location / Device → ABAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Classification → MAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owner → DAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🏗️ Example&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-example&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-example&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DAC → a file owner grants access to another user&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MAC → a secret-level document is only accessible to users with the matching clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RBAC → an HR role can access employee records&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ABAC → a finance manager can access reports only during business hours from the corporate network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;📚 References&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-references&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-references&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ISC2 CISSP CBK, Domain 5 – Identity and Access Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NIST SP 800-53, AC family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NIST SP 800-162, Guide to Attribute Based Access Control (ABAC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🔁 Quick Recall&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-quick-recall&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-quick-recall&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DAC = Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MAC = Label&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RBAC = Role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ABAC = Context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>[05] Account Termination and Deprovisioning</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/04_playbooks/cissp/d5/05-account-termination/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 30 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/04_playbooks/cissp/d5/05-account-termination/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;div style=&#34;margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #6b7280; display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px;&#34;&gt;
  
    &lt;span style=&#34;display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;&#34;&gt;
      By:
      
        
        
        
        
          
          
          
            
          
          
          &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/in/prasannavbalaji&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34; style=&#34;display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-weight: 600; color: #0a66c2; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;&#34; onmouseover=&#34;this.style.borderBottom=&#39;1px solid #0a66c2&#39;&#34; onmouseout=&#34;this.style.borderBottom=&#39;1px solid transparent&#39;&#34;&gt;
